  "answer_text": "Here is how you can log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd10 My Service Canada Account (MSCA) \u2013 Login\n\n**\ud83d\udc49 Direct Login Link:**\n[https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)\n\n---\n\n## Sign-In Options\n\nThere are **three ways** to sign in to MSCA:\n\n1. **GCKey**\nGCKey allows you to access multiple Government of Canada online services. You can use your GCKey username and password to log in.\n\n2. **Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner (Banking Credentials)**\nInterac\u00ae Sign-In Partner allows you to register or sign in using your online banking sign-in information to access MSCA.\n\n3. **Provincial Sign-In (Alberta & BC only)**\nYou can access My Service Canada Account (MSCA) by signing in or registering with your provincial sign-in. This service is only available for residents of Alberta and British Columbia.\n\n---\n\n## New User? Register Here\n\nIf you don't have an account yet:\n- By clicking \"Start your registration,\" you will be able to create a GCKey username and password if you don't already have one.\n- PACs (Personal Access Codes) are used to verify your identity when registering for MSCA. If you already applied for CPP/OAS benefits, your PAC has been sent to you by mail.\n\n---\n\n> \u26a0\ufe0f **Security Reminder:** Access and use MSCA only as yourself. No one is authorized to use or create an account on your behalf.\n\nIf you need further help, you can contact **Service Canada at 1-800-206-7218**.",
